# KNOWN GAP (R47 Track D1, found by the output-review) — the RECEIVER/ROOT-SHAPE
# axis of the primitive-receiver reject. The reject fires only when the receiver
# is a bare IDENTIFIER; every other spelling of the same `float` receiver still
# slips through.
#
# THIS IS THE SHARPEST CELL, which is why it is the committed repro: a CHAINED
# receiver does not merely mis-mint a slot, it invents the runtime symbol the
# reject exists to prevent —
#
#   RUST gg   : REJECTS — error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `to_string` found on
#               type `float`
#   SELF-HOST : ACCEPTS, then link-fails on
#               `undefined reference to 'int64_t__to_string'`
#
# That is verbatim the failure mode Rust's own reject site was written to stop
# ("the LIR `gorget_str_{method}` name-concat fallback invent[s] a bogus runtime
# symbol → ugly C error or silent miscompile"), reaching the link stage on the
# self-host lane.
#
# THE AXIS, ENUMERATED — all four non-identifier cells measured 2026-08-29
# against the post-D1 driver, Rust rejecting every one:
#
#   | receiver shape        | probe                     | self-host              |
#   |-----------------------|---------------------------|------------------------|
#   | identifier (CONTROL)  | `f.to_string()`           | REJECT  ← the only one |
#   | method-call result    | `mk().to_string()`        | CC-FAIL 'Str' from int |
#   | field access          | `h.v.to_string()`         | CC-FAIL 'Str' from int |
#   | chained call          | `f.mod(2.0).to_string()`  | LINK-FAIL (this file)  |
#   | index                 | `v[0].to_string()`        | CC-FAIL 'Str' from int |
#
# WHY THE REJECT IS BOUNDED THIS WAY, and why widening it is not a one-liner.
# `reject_no_method_on_primitive` refuses only when a SECOND, INDEPENDENT avenue
# corroborates the receiver's type — lexical scope lookup of the receiver's
# NAME. That filter exists because the self-host's span-keyed resolution answers
# a CONFIDENTLY WRONG type in measured cases, and without it the reject refused
# twelve valid corpus programs. A computed receiver has no name to look up, so
# there is no second avenue and the reject abstains rather than guess.
#
# ⇒ Closing this needs a corroboration story for computed receivers, OR the
# underlying resolution defect fixed so that one avenue is trustworthy on its
# own. Do NOT close it by dropping the corroboration filter — that is measured
# to refuse valid programs.
#
# CORRECT behaviour: `gg check` REJECTS this program on every lane.
void main():
    float f = 7.5
    print(f.mod(2.0).to_string())
